# Project: KU Rebate Management prototype (Pycube)

A prototype that runs alongside KU Medical Center's existing systems. Read `docs/ku-consignment-spec.md` for the workflow and `db/ku-schema.sql` for the data model before changing anything.

## Hard constraints (never break these)

1. NO patient identifiers anywhere: no MRN, name, DOB, encounter number, in any table, log, seed or UI. A "case" holds only department, room, procedure type and timestamps.
2. NO write-back. Pycube never sends anything to Epic, GE or Workday. KU data arrives only as file imports. Do not add integration code for those systems.
3. Build only what the current phase asks for. Container 1 (Consignment) is the first build. Container 2 (Consumption) is a thin close-out slice only. Container 3 (Contracts) is not built yet; its tables may exist but have no screens.
4. Every state change writes a row to `audit_log` (who, when, container, entity, action).
5. Every exception records `source_container` (1, 2 or 3).
6. KU decides and places orders. Pycube only shows information, alerts and recommendations. Never build an "order" or "purchase" action.

## Stack (change only if I say so)

- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript, SQLite via Drizzle ORM, Tailwind CSS
- Zod for validation; Vitest for tests
- Auth for the prototype: a simple user picker (no passwords), with roles: tech, supply_chain, category_owner, admin, vendor_rep

## Conventions

- All business logic lives in `src/lib/` as plain functions with unit tests, never inside route handlers or components.
- Stock on hand is DERIVED from `stock_events`, never stored: on_hand = arrived + returned - pulled - expired.
- Barcode parsing lives in one module, `src/lib/barcode.ts`. GS1 gives item, lot and expiry. HIBC gives the item only, so lot and expiry are entered manually in the prototype (photo reading is a later feature).
- A vendor_rep user may only ever see rows for their own vendor. Enforce this in the data-access layer, not just the UI.
- Dates are ISO strings. Quantities are integers for items.
- Seed data lives in `db/seed.ts` and uses placeholders such as "Vendor X". Mark any invented number as a placeholder in the UI footer.
- Small, reviewable commits: one phase per commit. Do not refactor unrelated code.

## Definition of done for any phase

- Types compile, tests pass, the screen works against seed data, and the audit_log shows the actions.
- No patient fields. No write-back code. Nothing outside the phase's scope.
